FILE: examples/shared/example.css
FEATURE: example-redesign
DATE: 2026-08-26
PRIOR STATE: did not exist

OLD_SECTION
(new file)

NEW_SECTION
166 lines: tokens (palette, mono/sans stacks) and primitives — .wrap, .hero (+ .eyebrow,
.hero-sub, .hero-cta, .hero-src), section/h2/.num/.lede/.note, .panel (+ .panel-h,
.panel-b, .dots), form controls (.field, label.lbl, textarea, select, range, color,
.row, .switch), buttons (.primary, .ghost, .tiny, .danger), .cards/.card, .status,
pre.snip, .log, .err-out, footer, .kbd, .pill.

REASON
The standard added under feature 'example-design-standard' applies to four pages. Without
a shared file each page would carry its own copy of the same ~170 lines, and "the examples
read as one set" would survive only as long as nobody edited one of them.

The split is tokens and primitives here, demo-specific rules in each page's own <style>.
That line is drawn at reusability, not at convenience: .panel and .card earn their place
because all four pages use them; the autowriter playground grid, the modal content
blocks, the SPA table and the form's axis-class layouts stay local because they mean
nothing anywhere else.

Linked directly by each page rather than through the library's asset loader
(vModel.core.functions.linkStyleSheet), because it belongs to the demos, not to vUX —
routing it through assetPath would imply the library ships it.
